6c6bffc7-20e9-569d-88cc-50d1ea81c42a.history:
Many archaeologists and specialists indicate the presence of four kingdoms in al-'Ula (Alula) which formed civilizations since the beginning of the sixth century BC, these kingdoms are:  
\- Kingdom of Dadan from the sixth century BC until the beginning of the fifth century BC;  
\-Kingdom of Lihyan and scientists identified the history of the state from the beginning of the fifth century BC until the end of the third century BC;  
\- State of Maeen which was presence in the region from the middle of the sixth century BC and lasted until the beginning of the first century AD;  
\- Nabataeans state: The Nabataeans were Arab tribes lived in the area between Iraq, Syria and Jordan, and came to the area of Petra in Jordan and seized it from the Edomites. Nabataeans reached an advanced stage of sophisticated culture before the Roman occupation of Syria in 65 BC, and then the fall of the kingdom in 206 AD.
